= Pulse =

== Overview ==
A '''pulse''' is the rhythmic pressure wave associated with heartbeats and is commonly used to measure heart rate as beats per minute.

== Definition ==
In routine clinical use, pulse or heart rate is the number of heartbeats in a period of time, usually one minute. A pulse can be felt where an artery passes near the skin.

== Scope & importance ==
Pulse measurement is a basic vital-sign observation. Rate, rhythm, and context can provide information about cardiovascular function and physiological state.

== Core concepts ==
Common pulse sites include the wrist and neck. Heart rate varies with age, activity, body position, medications, temperature, fitness, stress, and health conditions.

== Examples ==
A clinician may count the radial pulse at the wrist. Wearable sensors can estimate pulse rate optically, while an electrocardiogram measures cardiac electrical activity by a different method.

== Applications / implications ==
Pulse is used in routine examinations, exercise monitoring, emergency assessment, inpatient care, and many physiological measurements.

== Epistemic notes ==
A pulse value is context-dependent and is not a diagnosis by itself. Measurement method, rhythm irregularity, activity state, symptoms, and individual factors affect interpretation.

